From 3b98c14e29bdbfa86ad36a7a43cda6494f9172ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chris <08a487@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:44:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 26/28] iommu/qcom: Disable the clocks again when resume fails

qcom_iommu_resume() enables the clocks and then, for an IOMMU in a
power domain, asks the secure world to restore its configuration. When
that call failed, the error went back to runtime PM with the clocks
still enabled, and every later attempt took another reference: on
MSM8994, where the call failed at first, each probe of the GPU SMMU's
context bank left the GPU core and AHB clocks enabled once more.

Undo the clock enable when the secure configuration fails.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 21d18ce67..ef2cf87ba 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -899,8 +899,11 @@ static int __maybe_unused qcom_iommu_resume(struct device *dev)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (dev->pm_domain)
-		return qcom_scm_restore_sec_cfg(qcom_iommu->sec_id, 0);
+	if (dev->pm_domain) {
+		ret = qcom_scm_restore_sec_cfg(qcom_iommu->sec_id, 0);
+		if (ret)
+			clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(CLK_NUM, qcom_iommu->clks);
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
